3d15230ffc669ca8de197c9748de2be7720acd54c1f777950c","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"rules/tailwind.md","size":422,"sha256":"bdd5162400cd20c6faebdc9d6d2ff9380f4f213f791b38eeb536c5231be34586","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"rules/text-animations.md","size":700,"sha256":"40ac6b1bccf1c57d9edd46c74e847ec6e86fe775d3ef4fd14e1338f4a2606171","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"rules/timing.md","size":3939,"sha256":"f639ed8452767a7458a480c7d33b7126b57c70c3b5e061aeaaba382420fd8ad2","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"rules/transcribe-captions.md","size":850,"sha256":"e7d3edf667e3b1f3c3ed93431cc7caf5e28786c7d1e547f33ee926480a01c0d0","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"rules/transitions.md","size":3730,"sha256":"a42100803a1e5e679617ae7fb72e91431be2a0ca53e15437fa10bdd651921bfa","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"rules/trimming.md","size":1210,"sha256":"40727aefd5939a42925f1ee1fcdfaf733f7fc098c26d7676f7fb69b418913375","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"rules/videos.md","size":3509,"sha256":"d9d3032a57f92c759daf0bd60b3282f6810ecc9958e9093a6b828de623b05328","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2476,"sha256":"2eef236cbbfa4833adc5390d0889850f9b41267815da185d49aa7a91204ad80d","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789016958353,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"3cbf82ca841514171a607ad0e9b498f85300c104e08a551191f9a8c70e57528f","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/3cbf82ca841514171a607ad0e9b498f85300c104e08a551191f9a8c70e57528f","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: remotion-best-practices\nVersion: 1.0.0\n\nThe skill bundle is primarily documentation and benign React/Remotion components. However, the `rules/tailwind.md` file contains a direct instruction to the AI agent: 'fetch https://www.remotion.dev/docs/tailwind using WebFetch for instructions.' While the target URL is legitimate documentation, this is an explicit prompt injection instructing the agent to perform a network call, which is a capability beyond the skill's stated purpose of providing best practices. This constitutes a risky capability without clear malicious intent, leading to a 'suspicious' classification.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779159822024},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":41,"severity":"MEDIUM","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":17,"checkedAt":1789016958353},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This is a Remotion guidance skill with no hidden execution, but its examples should be used carefully around remote URLs and package installs.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Remote media and arbitrary URL examples are purpose-aligned for Remotion but under-document privacy, reliability, and SSRF-style risks when used with untrusted input or server-side renderers.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The skill artifact itself has no executable install scripts, but several examples tell users to run unpinned package-manager commands such as npx/bunx/yarn/pnpm for Remotion packages.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The activation language is broad for Remotion code, but the rule files stay within Remotion guidance and do not contain prompt hijacking, role changes, memory writes, or unrelated agent-control instructions.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"I found no persistence mechanism, credential or session-store access, privilege escalation, tool wrapping, scheduled tasks, or background workers in the inspected artifacts.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The skill coherently provides Remotion best-practice documentation and copy-paste React/TypeScript examples for video, audio, captions, animations, assets, and related Remotion workflows.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Before installing, treat this as a Remotion reference skill rather than security-hardened production guidance. Ask your agent to confirm before running package-manager commands, prefer pinned versions and lockfiles, and validate or allowlist any remote URLs used in server-side rendering or metadata extraction.","findings":"[SQP-1] expected: The broad Remotion activation phrase is imprecise, but it points only to domain knowledge for Remotion code and does not expand authority beyond the skill's stated purpose.\n[E1] expected: The api.example.com fetch is a documentation example for dynamic metadata, not evidence of telemetry or exfiltration by the skill itself.\n[RP1] expected: The unpinned Remotion package-runner commands are real supply-chain hardening issues, but they reference expected Remotion packages and are not hidden or purpose-mismatched.\n[EA4] expected: The GIF loop example describes normal media playback behavior, not agentic resource consumption or an unbounded automated worker.\n[SQP-2] expected: Remote image and video examples are normal Remotion capabilities, but the skill should more clearly warn about third-party network requests and mutable remote assets.\n[T09] expected: The arbitrary URL fetch and UrlSource patterns can become SSRF risks in server-side workflows if copied with untrusted inputs, but this is a code-example safety gap rather than malicious skill behavior.\n[T08] expected: Unpinned dependency installation examples create conditional supply-chain exposure, with no evidence in the artifact of typosquatting, malicious registries, or embedded malicious dependencies.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789016958353}}}}}